<Page title={`About ${site.BRAND}: Who We Are and How This Site Works`} description={`${site.BRAND} publishes free, practical guides on this topic: real numbers, real sources, and tools that replace guesswork instead of filler.`}>
  <p>{site.BRAND} is an independent site. {site.author.bio}</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>Food storage guides tend to either panic people into buying everything at once or stay so vague they're useless. We publish specific shelf-life windows by food type, rotation schedules, and the actual water and calorie totals a household needs per person per day, based on USDA and FEMA emergency preparedness figures rather than round numbers someone guessed at.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Shelf-life and storage figures come from USDA FoodKeeper data and FEMA and Red Cross emergency supply guidance. Guides are drafted with AI assistance and checked against those sources before publishing; the process is described in our <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a>. Where storage life depends on packaging method, oxygen absorbers versus vacuum seal, we list both instead of picking one.</p>

  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>Every guide here is free. We earn affiliate commissions when readers buy storage containers, freeze-dried food, or preparedness kits through links on this site. Full terms are in our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If a shelf-life figure or calorie estimate looks wrong, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. We correct it and note the date.</p>
</Page>
